        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does kitty litter really work on driveway oil?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It does on fresh spills, on both asphalt and concrete. Plain clay litter soaks up free oil well, particularly when you grind it in with your shoe so the granules crumble and reach into the surface texture. It does little for an old, set-in stain, because by then the oil has moved down below the surface where litter cannot get at it."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is dish soap safe on an asphalt driveway?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Grease-cutting dish soap is among the safest cleaners for blacktop, because it is water-based and leaves the asphalt binder alone. Use plenty of it, scrub with a nylon brush, give it about 15 minutes and rinse well. It handles fresh and light stains; heavier ones generally call for a water-based degreaser or an enzyme cleaner."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I use the same degreaser on asphalt and concrete?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Only when the label says it is safe on asphalt. Many alkaline, water-based degreasers qualify, but solvent-based and citrus solvent products do not. If you are unsure, try a small spot near the edge of the driveway, let it dry and check for softening, tackiness or loose stone before you treat the main stain."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does it take to get oil off a driveway?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "About one evening for a fresh spill on either surface: absorbent overnight, then roughly 30 minutes of cleaning the next day. A stain that has sat on concrete for weeks may take two or three rounds spread over several days. On asphalt, an enzyme cleaner can need a week to finish, though it asks very little of you in the meantime."
