            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "They can. Oil softens the asphalt binder, and a stain left for weeks can leave a patch that crumbles or stays tacky. Small spots that get cleaned up usually recover once the area is primed and sealed. Larger soft areas should be cut out and filled with cold patch asphalt before you seal the driveway."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is it safe to rinse oil cleaner into the street?",
