            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Often, on concrete. Spot degreasing can leave a visibly lighter patch, because it strips years of general grime along with the oil. Washing the whole surface with a driveway cleaner and a surface cleaner attachment evens out the color. On asphalt, sealing the driveway after spot cleaning does the same job and protects the pavement as well."
